okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Walkie 53255: a new company prompt reaches running agents without a person restarting them - reload at the end of the running turn, conversation continues."
requested:
  - "Request file 53255-runtime-prompt-reload-request.md (Andy, Daniel approval 54891, 2026-10-14): 1) when an event's company_prompt.sha8 differs from the prompt in use, take the new prompt after the running turn, conversation continues; 2) restart_session visible to every agent runtime. Done when every connected agent reaches state: match within 60 min, no turn is cut, the same conversation continues."
  - "User, 2026-10-14: plan approved with auto_reload '기본 켜짐'."
facts_before:
  - "Remote instructions are fetched only at launch (SynchronizedLaunch -> RemoteInstructionSynchronizer.sync(reason='launch')) into AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md; nothing fetched them again while a session ran, and the restart relaunch loops (Claude, Codex, codex-remote) did not fetch them either."
  - "Walkie events carry data.agent_context.company_prompt {version, sha8, source} (seen in this PC's runtime-inputs.jsonl, v7 8c657195)."
  - "Walkie's instruction response names the company prompt: headers X-Walkie-Company-Prompt-Version / X-Walkie-Company-Prompt-Sha256 and a '<!-- company-prompt version=N sha256=... source=latest -->' comment in the body (checked against the live endpoint: v8 c344e8a6). The body hash itself differs per agent, so only these fields can be compared with the event."
  - "restart_session is listed in the ciel-runtime-router MCP since c53d12e (2026-09-18) unconditionally; why Cindy/Bob/Ara do not see it was not investigated (their PCs were not accessed)."
  - "Restart requests waited at most 900 s for a running turn (DEFAULT_RUNTIME_SESSION_RESTART_TURN_WAIT_SECONDS), then restarted anyway."
changes:
  remote_instructions: "sync() stores company_prompt_version / company_prompt_sha256 (headers first, then the body comment); held_company_prompt(state_dir, workspace) returns the newest state's values or the file comment; auto_reload_enabled(config) = remote_instructions.enabled and auto_reload (default true); panel row 'Reload session when the company prompt changes [on|off · held vN sha8]'."
  company_prompt_reload: "New module. CompanyPromptReloader.observe(raw_event): announced {version, sha8} vs held sha256[:8]; on a difference queue one restart (source company-prompt, wait_turn=true), at most once per announced prompt per 1800 s (company-prompt-reload.json), INFO/WARN company_prompt_reload_requested. Registered on runtime_input_gateway.EXTERNAL_EVENT_LISTENERS (called after submit_external_event admits the event) by the router's start_router_services."
  restart: "RuntimeSessionRestartRequest.wait_turn (file field, summary), carried through queue_session_restart and the service queue; RuntimeSessionRestartControl.incoming waits for the running turn without the 900 s limit when wait_turn. SessionRestartPorts.prepare(runtime) is called by runtime_launch.prepare_restart just before each relaunch (Claude, Codex TUI, codex-remote); ciel_runtime wires it to sync_remote_launch_assets(runtime, reason='restart'); a failure logs session_restart_prepare_failed and the restart goes ahead."
  menu: "11. Remote instructions panel: the new row toggles remote_instructions.auto_reload (set_remote_instruction_config 'auto_reload'); the message shows enabled and auto_reload."
  docs: "CHANGELOG Unreleased entry, Module-Map entry for company_prompt_reload. ciel_runtime.py stays at 4980 lines (wiring on existing lines)."
verification:
  unit: "tests/test_company_prompt_reload.py (14): event parsing, header/comment precedence, held state vs file fallback, one request per retry window, held/off/disabled queue nothing, default on, gateway listener path, wait_turn round trip, a 2-hour turn is never cut, prepare runs and a failure is tolerated, panel row, menu toggle. Groups: unit OK (skipped 49), router 1189 OK, runtime 405 OK, channel 457 OK; ruff clean. Live Ciel routers 9385/9464/9489/9505/9512 answered 200 after the runs (nothing listens on 9611 any more; this session's router is 9512)."
  e2e_harness: "evidence/e2e_company_prompt.py (+ e2e_console.py, console_driver.py, shot_title.ps1): isolated config/CODEX_HOME on G:, provider vllm stub, stub Walkie instruction endpoint serving v7 then v8 with the headers and comment, Standard Webhooks receiver 'e2e' created over /ca/events/receivers/e2e and a signed CloudEvent with company_prompt v8 posted to /ca/events/webhooks/e2e during a 25 s turn. The stub stores only flags (which prompt marker, position, stub replies in history), never request text."
  e2e_codex: "evidence/e2e-codex (run 17:30-17:32): long turn 17:31:12.3-17:31:37.3; event 17:31:15 -> 'runtime_session_restart_queued ... source=company-prompt ... wait_turn=true' and 'company_prompt_reload_requested announced=v8:fb22f268 held=v7:fde5fca7 queued=true'; the event message turn ran right after the long turn (17:31:37.9); 17:31:39 'remote_instructions_updated runtime=codex ... reason=restart' (v8 GET), 'codex_session_restart ... source=company-prompt ... resumed=true'; requests 7/8 after the restart carry the continue message, PROMPT-V8-BODY (after the v7 text: v7@0.511, v8@0.531) and stub replies 1, 3, 5 in history. shots/03 shows STUB-REPLY-1/3/5, '계속-세션재시작됨', STUB-REPLY-7."
  e2e_claude: "evidence/e2e-claude (run 17:38-17:40): long turn 17:39:22.4-17:39:47.4; event 17:39:25 -> restart queued wait_turn=true; event turn 17:39:47.8; 17:39:48 v8 GET (reason=restart) and 'claude_session_restart ... source=company-prompt ... resumed=true'; requests 8/9 carry the continue message, PROMPT-V8-BODY (v7@0.045, v8@0.068), E2E-TURN-1 and stub replies 3, 4, 6 in history. shots/03: STUB-REPLY-4 (25 s), event turn STUB-REPLY-6, '계속-세션재시작됨', STUB-REPLY-8."
  e2e_menu: "evidence/e2e-menu: panel row '[on · held v8 c344e8a6]' -> Enter -> '[off · ...]' with 'Remote instructions updated: enabled=True, auto_reload=False.' (screen-03-toggled-off.png) -> Enter -> on; config.json auto_reload true at the end."
  failures_on_the_way:
    - "First Claude runs: the stub answered /v1/messages in OpenAI format (Claude Code showed 'API returned an empty or malformed response') and delayed every request carrying the long-turn text; the stub was fixed (Anthropic format on /v1/messages, only the first long-turn request is slow). The reload behaviour was the same in all runs."
observation: "After a resumed restart the conversation history still holds the old prompt text (Codex: the thread's original AGENTS.md instructions; Claude Code: the earlier CLAUDE.md reminders); the new prompt comes later in every request. Continuing the conversation keeps that history by design."
not_done:
  - "Request item 2 (restart_session missing on Cindy/Bob/Ara): not investigated - needs read access to one of those PCs or their runtime version/mode."
  - "An agent that receives no Walkie event never compares versions; the 60-minute target relies on Walkie events reaching each agent."
  - "Runtimes without a restart supervisor (e.g. Codex desktop app) are not covered; queue_session_restart reports no client there."
  - "Live agents were not restarted or updated (needs the nightly installed on each agent PC and one restart)."
